This is one you may never run into but if you do I have programmed in a fix 
for it.  If you have installed the BBSTEXT enhancements for Gfiles/Pfiles/News
found in CNetToolkit (by Dotoran and PMK) for Split display with Ansi boxes, 
AND you have a more prompt that rotates, or does something else flashy, rather
than just the standard more prompt, it can crash the port so you should add 
the following tidbits of code to the line in bbstext which calls the more 
prompt. (Line 1064) <If you have changed the 'Changewhere' setting that is
preset for a user in Pfiles to something other than 'Pfiles' then the word
'Pfiles' below should be changed to your setting.  It is case sensitive so
make certain it is identical.>

   +-----Add This---------+                    +----Add This----+
\q2{t1601730 #Pfiles}{je 1} Flashy prompt code {1}More [Y,n,c]\q3

\=Ctrl-y  {=Ctrl-q

This code will check to see if the user is in Pfiles.  If they are, they will
use a standard more prompt rather than a rotating one, thus skipping the 
chance for a crash.


